.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Theodore Maiman&#x27;s 1960 ruby laser used a resonator formed by two mirrors bounding an amplifying medium -- precisely the kind of optical cavity that ray-transfer matrix theory was soon developed to analyze. This package does not model laser gain media, but spherical_mirror and cavity_round_trip_matrix build the ABCD round-trip matrix of a two-mirror resonator like Maiman&#x27;s, and cavity_stability tests whether such a cavity traps light indefinitely (a stable resonator, |A+D| \le 2) or walks rays out of the cavity on successive round trips.">

